    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "What is the difference between the speed and velocity of a particle’s motion?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Speed is the non-negative rate of distance travelled. Velocity is the signed rate of change of displacement; speed is $|v|$.",
      "worked": "Velocity is $v=\\dfrac{dx}{dt}$ and can be positive, negative or zero. Speed is $|v|$, so it gives how fast the particle moves without its direction.",
